WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.491
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:04.791 --> 00:00:07.852
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.152 --> 00:00:14.799
Unit twenty-three: Health Care. In this unit, you will talk about medical visits and report questions.

4
00:00:15.783 --> 00:00:16.738
appointment.

5
00:00:17.438 --> 00:00:20.773
appointment means an arranged time to see a doctor or other person.

6
00:00:21.073 --> 00:00:23.304
I have a doctor's appointment at ten o'clock.

7
00:00:24.004 --> 00:00:26.459
Your turn. Say: appointment.

8
00:00:29.159 --> 00:00:30.184
appointment.

9
00:00:31.183 --> 00:00:32.289
diagnosis.

10
00:00:32.989 --> 00:00:37.032
diagnosis means the doctor's decision about what illness someone has.

11
00:00:37.332 --> 00:00:39.598
The diagnosis was a mild infection.

12
00:00:40.298 --> 00:00:42.765
Your turn. Say: diagnosis.

13
00:00:45.465 --> 00:00:46.791
diagnosis.

14
00:00:47.783 --> 00:00:48.819
specialist.

15
00:00:49.519 --> 00:00:53.388
specialist means a doctor with expert knowledge of one area of medicine.

16
00:00:53.688 --> 00:00:55.873
My doctor sent me to a heart specialist.

17
00:00:56.573 --> 00:00:59.051
Your turn. Say: specialist.

18
00:01:01.751 --> 00:01:02.880
specialist.

19
00:01:03.883 --> 00:01:04.559
treatment.

20
00:01:05.259 --> 00:01:07.770
treatment means medical care to cure an illness.

21
00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:09.825
The treatment lasted two weeks.

22
00:01:10.525 --> 00:01:12.934
Your turn. Say: treatment.

23
00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:16.380
treatment.

24
00:01:17.383 --> 00:01:18.280
side effect.

25
00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:21.757
side effect means an unwanted effect of a medicine.

26
00:01:22.057 --> 00:01:25.113
A common side effect of this medicine is tiredness.

27
00:01:25.813 --> 00:01:28.361
Your turn. Say: side effect.

28
00:01:31.061 --> 00:01:32.097
side effect.

29
00:01:33.083 --> 00:01:33.922
symptom.

30
00:01:34.622 --> 00:01:37.887
symptom means a sign of an illness, like a fever or a cough.

31
00:01:38.187 --> 00:01:40.721
A high temperature is a common symptom of flu.

32
00:01:41.421 --> 00:01:43.608
Your turn. Say: symptom.

33
00:01:46.308 --> 00:01:47.251
symptom.

34
00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:49.390
medical record.

35
00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:53.495
medical record means official notes about a person's health history.

36
00:01:53.795 --> 00:01:55.736
The nurse checked my medical record.

37
00:01:56.436 --> 00:01:59.158
Your turn. Say: medical record.

38
00:02:01.858 --> 00:02:03.080
medical record.

39
00:02:04.083 --> 00:02:05.061
prescription.

40
00:02:05.761 --> 00:02:08.666
prescription means a doctor's written order for medicine.

41
00:02:08.966 --> 00:02:10.954
Take this prescription to the pharmacy.

42
00:02:11.654 --> 00:02:14.330
Your turn. Say: prescription.

43
00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:18.019
prescription.

44
00:02:19.017 --> 00:02:21.121
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:21.421 --> 00:02:23.049
How was your appointment at the clinic?

46
00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:27.629
Fine. The doctor asked me how long I'd had the headaches.

47
00:02:28.917 --> 00:02:30.254
What else did she ask?

48
00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:34.107
She asked whether I was taking any medicine.

49
00:02:35.417 --> 00:02:37.358
Did she give you a diagnosis?

50
00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:42.893
Not yet. She asked about my symptoms and gave me a prescription.

51
00:02:44.183 --> 00:02:46.903
Grammar focus: Reported questions.

52
00:02:47.203 --> 00:02:51.118
To report a question, use asked, then a question word or if.

53
00:02:51.418 --> 00:02:54.056
Use normal word order and move the tense back.

54
00:02:54.356 --> 00:02:57.368
For example: Do you smoke? He asked if I smoked.

55
00:02:57.668 --> 00:03:02.059
Reported questions are not real questions: no question mark and no do / does / did.

56
00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:05.633
Now read and listen. Health Care Close to Home.

57
00:03:05.933 --> 00:03:09.801
In many rural areas, the nearest hospital can be hours away.

58
00:03:11.117 --> 00:03:14.289
Local clinics now offer basic treatment and health checks.

59
00:03:15.583 --> 00:03:18.825
Doctors keep a medical record for every patient on a tablet.

60
00:03:20.117 --> 00:03:23.509
Patients who need a specialist can talk to one by video call.

61
00:03:24.817 --> 00:03:28.012
This helps with early diagnosis and a faster recovery.

62
00:03:29.317 --> 00:03:31.760
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:34.536
An unwanted effect of a medicine is a blank.

64
00:03:34.836 --> 00:03:39.453
A, side effect. B, diagnosis. C, recovery.

65
00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:45.368
The answer is A: side effect.

66
00:03:46.883 --> 00:03:50.128
"Are you tired?" → She asked if I blank tired.

67
00:03:50.428 --> 00:03:53.245
A, am. B, was. C, were being.

68
00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.331
The answer is B: was.

69
00:04:00.817 --> 00:04:02.282
He asked me where I blank.

70
00:04:02.582 --> 00:04:05.353
A, work. B, worked. C, did work.

71
00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:10.815
The answer is B: worked.

72
00:04:12.317 --> 00:04:15.384
A doctor with expert knowledge of one area is a blank.

73
00:04:15.684 --> 00:04:18.989
A, specialist. B, clinic. C, waiting room.

74
00:04:22.983 --> 00:04:25.250
The answer is A: specialist.

75
00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:30.120
According to the text, patients can talk to specialists by blank.

76
00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:33.934
A, letter. B, video call. C, radio.

77
00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:39.717
The answer is B: video call.

78
00:04:41.217 --> 00:04:45.169
Now it's your turn to speak. What questions does a doctor usually ask you?

79
00:04:50.469 --> 00:04:56.927
The doctor usually asks what my symptoms are, how long I have had them and whether I have any allergies.

80
00:04:57.227 --> 00:04:58.971
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:04:59.983 --> 00:05:03.994
Great work today! You learned eight new words and reported questions.

82
00:05:04.294 --> 00:05:07.864
Today's value is healthy body. Move your body every day.

83
00:05:08.164 --> 00:05:10.886
See you in Unit twenty-four. Goodbye!

84
00:05:11.186 --> 00:05:14.035
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

